<header class="major"><h1>D-MART Sales & Profit Performance Dashboard</h1></header>

<h3>Problem:</h3>
<p>D-MART was making sales across 10 cities, but managers were deciding from scattered Excel sheets.<br>
No one could answer in 10 seconds:<br>
Which city is winning?<br>
Which category makes profit?<br>
Why do sales dip?</p>

<h3>Solution:</h3>
<p>I built a fully interactive Power BI dashboard with filters for Date, City, Store, Category, and Payment Method.<br>
One page, all answers.</p>
<p>Built with: Power BI | DAX | Data Modelling | Interactive Slicers</p>

<h3>Key Findings:</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Profit:</strong> 1M Sales, 233K Profit, 22% Margin, 5K Quantity</li>
<li><strong>Category:</strong> Grocery 279K / 62K profit is the engine. Home Care 211K / 48K and Beverages 192K / 43K follow. Snacks 8K / 2K and Bakery 16K / 4K are dragging.</li>
<li><strong>City:</strong> Eldoret 127K, Nakuru 122K, Kiambu 121K lead. Mombasa 83K and Kisumu 75K lag.</li>
<li><strong>Payment:</strong> M-PESA 298K, Credit Card 294K, Cash 238K, Debit Card 221K - 56% is already digital.</li>
<li><strong>Season:</strong> Peak March 105K & Dec 101K. Dip July 71K & Feb 73K.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Recommendations:</h3>
<ol>
<li>Stock more in Eldoret, Nakuru, Kiambu</li>
<li>Re-price, bundle or replace Snacks & Bakery</li>
<li>Make checkout mobile-first for M-PESA & Card</li>
<li>Stock up in Feb for March peak, run promo in June/July for the dip</li>
</ol>

<h3>Impact:</h3>
<p>A manager can now filter by their city in the morning and know where to send stock today.<br>
That's reporting turned into decision-making.</p>

